ertificate Chains\nDescription: As originally announced on May 18, 2023 and November 2, 2023, weak client certificate chains have been deprecated for the region eu20 in order to harden security standards.   Accordingly, the OpenSSL security has been raised to level 2, resulting in weak certificates or certificate chains no longer being accepted by the platform. For more information and a full definition of security level 2, see https://www.openssl.org/docs/man3.0\",751\n189,\" Regular Upgrade\nDescription: Identity Authentication has been upgraded.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2024-01-04\nValid as Of: 2024-01-04\nVersion: 25446\n\n--- Record 3686 ---\nComponent: Documentation\nEnvironment: ABAP,Cloud Foundry,Kyma,Neo,Other\nTitle: Use of Comments for Feedback\nDescription: You can now add comments to provide feedback directly on SAP Help Portal for the SAP Business Technology Platform and SAP BTP, Neo Environment documentation. See Giving Feedback on SAP Documentation and Creating Better Documentation Together: SAP Help Portal’s new approach to Collaboration and Feedback.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2024-01-04\nValid as Of: 2024-01-04\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 3687 ---\nComponent: Responsibility Management Service\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Import Teams\nDescription: You can now import teams from SAP S/4HANA Cloud to the Manage Teams and Responsibilities app. For more information, seeImport Teams.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: Announcement\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2024-01-01\nValid as Of: 2024-01-04\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 3688 ---\nComponent: Kyma Runtime\nEnvironment: Kyma\nTitle: SAP BTP Operator module: Update to version 1.1.0\nDescription: With this release, we have updated the SAP BTP service operator resources to version 0.5.6. We have introduced a new feature that allows you to create a Service Instance with a custom Secret. For more details and instructions, go to Use BTP Manager to Manage SAP BTP Service Operator.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2023-12-20\nValid as Of: 2024-01-03\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 3689 ---\nComponent: SAP Build Process Automation\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Store - New Content Packages\nDescription: A new set of 19 content packages - 12 Business Content and 7 Learning Content - were added to the Store during December 2023. We have also made some fixes to the existing content packages.  These content packages are tailored to different lines of business such as IT, Sales, Services, Sourcing, Finance, and Procurement.  SAP S/4HANA Business Content:  Automatic Sales Order Creation via Email using Excel.  Mass Fixed Asset Acquisition.  Inactive Vendor Mark for Blockage or Deletion.  Creation of Supplier Invoice by Reference Invoice.  Duplicate Supplier Request Rejection.  Create Customer Material Info Records.  Mass Maintenance of Purchasing Info Records.  Mass Completion of Supplier Quotations & Request for Quotations.  Mass Creation of Bank Master.  Mass Purchase Orders Closure.  Mass Creation of Measuring Documents.  Mass Processing of Planned Orders.    Learning Content:  Sales Order Management (MI01).  Sales Order Management (MI02).  Sales Order Management (MI03).  Sales Order Management (MI04).  Sales Order Management (MI05).  Sales Order Management (MI06).  Sales Order Management (MI07).    Updated Content:  Activation Accelerators - In-App Configuration for SAP S4HANA Cloud Scope item J59 (6PS) (SAP S/4HANA).  Automated Purchase Order Upload (2R2) (SAP Business By Design).  \nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2024-01-01\nValid as Of: 2024-01-01\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 3690 ---\nComponent: SAP Conversational AI\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: SAP Conversational AI Community Edition\nDescription: SAP Conversational AI community edition will no longer be available after December 31, 2023. Licensed users can migrate productive bots to the enterprise edition of the platform to ensure un-interrupted conversation experience for your users. See Import your Bots from the Community Tenant.\nAction: Required\nLifecycle: Deprecated\nType: Announcement\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2023-07-05\nValid as Of: 2023-12-31\nVersion: Cloud\n\n\",566\n399,\"--- Record 141 ---\nComponent: Cloud Integration\nEnvironment: Neo\nTitle: Software Version Update\nDescription:   SAP Cloud Integration: 5.77.*    Adapter Development Kit for SAP Cloud Integration: 2.53.*      Increment: 2507    \nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: Changed\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2025-09-07\nValid as Of: 2025-09-07\nVersion: 2507\n\n--- Record 142 ---\nComponent: Cloud Integration\nEnvironment: Neo\nTitle: Software Version Update\nDescription:   SAP Cloud Integration: 7.42.*    Adapter Development Kit for SAP Cloud Integration: 2.53.*      Increment: 2507      The software version 7.42.* is being rolled out in a phased approach. All tenants running on software version 5.76.* would be automatically moved to 7.42.* or a higher version available at that point of time, in the near future.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: Changed\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2025-09-07\nValid as Of: 2025-09-07\nVersion: 2507\n\n--- Record 143 ---\nComponent: Cloud Integration\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry,Neo\nTitle: Streaming option for HTTP Receiver Adapter Available\nDescription: You can now split a large composite message for HTTP Receiver Adapter by streaming.  See HTTP Receiver Adapter  SAP Cloud Integration customers, see HTTP Receiver Adapter\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2025-09-07\nValid as Of: 2025-09-07\nVersion: 2507\n\n--- Record 144 ---\nComponent: Integration Advisor\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry,Neo\nTitle: Changed Behavior When Assigning Codelists to Leaf Nodes\nDescription: The behavior of the checkbox Use all code values of the codelist during the assignment of codelists to leaf nodes has been changed: If you manually select all code values of a list one by one without selecting the checkbox, the checkbox is no longer checked automatically.   This behavior has consequences, for example, if you migrate your MIG to a new message version and the new version provides more code values: If you didn't select the checkbox, each code value is migrated by itself, and any new code values stay unselected.  See Assigning Codelists to Leaf Nodes.  As Cloud Integration (standalone) customer, see Assigning Codelists to Leaf Nodes.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: Changed\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2025-09-07\nValid as Of: 2025-09-07\nVersion: 2507\n\n--- Record 145 ---\nComponent: Integration Advisor\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry,Neo\nTitle: Global Parameter Suggestions\nDescription: When creating global parameters inside a MAG, you're now provided with suggestions for frequently used parameters. This makes the creation of global parameters more convenient.  See Working with Mapping Guidelines.  As Cloud Integration (standalone) customer, see Working with Mapping Guidelines.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: Changed\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2025-09-07\nValid as Of: 2025-09-07\nVersion: 2507\n\n--- Record 146 ---\nComponent: Integration Advisor\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry,Neo\nTitle: Setting the UN/EDIFACT Message Version (Field 0052) for Older UN/EDIFACT Versions\nDescription: In your MIGs, you can now define the expected UN/EDIFACT message version value. The default value D is applied automaticall